{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Unto Moses and unto Aaron.</b> It said <b>and unto Aaron</b> — perhaps it intends to make both of them together emissaries for this commandment unto Israel, and so it concluded by saying <b>Speak unto the children of Israel</b>. And so it says in the portion of Bo (Exodus 12:1): ״אֶל מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן וגו׳ דַּבֵּרוּ״ וגו׳. For regarding the matter of precedence, that Moses should speak to Aaron before [speaking to] Israel, we have already learned this from another place." "<b>Saying unto them.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Torat Kohanim): ״אֲלֵיהֶם״ — meaning that he should say it to Elazar and to Itamar, and the intention of this is to give them precedence in learning first, as is taught (Eruvin 54a) in the order of study. Or perhaps it intends to require them to instruct the children of Israel, in the manner of (Malachi 2:7): ״כִּי שִׂפְתֵי כֹהֵן״ וגו׳, and therefore it juxtaposed to this ״דַּבֵּרוּ״ וגו׳. It will further be explained, the verse's saying <b>saying unto them</b>, according to what I explained in other places (Exodus 20:1), that the reason for saying ״לֵאמֹר״ is that the utterance going forth from the mouth of El Elyon would generate from itself an angel, and it was he who spoke with Moses, and the meaning of ״לֵאמֹר״ is: the utterance shall say [it] to Moses. And so here too it says ״לֵאמֹר אֲלֵיהֶם״ — meaning the utterance shall say [it] to Moses and to Aaron. And this explanation does not contradict the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory who said (Torat Kohanim 1) that the utterance was only to Moses and not to Aaron, for even according to our way, none heard the words of HaShem except Moses; rather, the angel that materialized from the utterance would speak in the plural tongue, and Moses would convey the matters to Aaron."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:04.718769482Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}